# Ignore skill contents (not the dir itself) so the committed project skills
# below can be re-included — git can't un-ignore a file whose parent DIR is
# ignored, but it can when only the dir's contents are.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/drain-loop.md
!.claude/skills/phase-run.md
.claude/start-*.sh
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.superpowers/
skills-lock.json

# Local scratch
tmp/

# Local Supabase stack, from `supabase init` in a worktree when verifying UI
# that needs Auth + Storage (the disposable test Postgres is not enough).
# Machine-specific: ports get shifted per worktree to let stacks coexist.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED, and it has to be. Unanchored, `supabase/` matches a directory
# at ANY depth — including `packages/db/src/supabase/` and
# `apps/web/src/lib/supabase/`, which are source. That is not hypothetical: it
# silently swallowed `packages/db/src/supabase/storage-stream.ts` from a
# `git add -A`, and the failure surfaced only in CI, as
# `Could not resolve "./supabase/storage-stream"` while every local check was
# green (local tooling tests the WORKING TREE; CI tests the COMMIT).
#
# It hid for so long because .gitignore only affects UNTRACKED files: the eight
# files already tracked in that directory kept working, so the directory looked
# tracked and nothing flagged that a ninth would not be.
/supabase/

# Stray screenshots dropped at the repo root by UI/design sessions.
# Root-scoped (leading slash) so committed images under .claude/artifacts/
# and apps/ are unaffected.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# CI-only Supabase project dir created by .github/workflows/stripe-e2e.yml
.supabase-ci/
